 ## Background
-Safe Raymarching Step Size originated from the need to render distorted Signed Distance Fields, such as those created by domain repetition or boolean operations, which can cause artifacts if the step size exceeds the local distance [S1, unofficial]. The method was formalized in implementations like the DIST-Renderer, which introduced clamping and ratio-based step control to stabilize differentiable rendering [S2, unofficial]. It is also referenced in collaborative neural radiance field implementations for novel view synthesis, where grid-based step sizes are calculated from AABB dimensions [S3, unofficial].
+Safe Raymarching Step Size originated from the need to render distorted Signed Distance Fields, such as those created by domain repetition or boolean operations, which can cause artifacts if the step size exceeds the local distance [S1, unofficial]. The method was formalized in implementations like the SDFRenderer, which introduced clamping and ratio-based step control to stabilize differentiable rendering [S2, unofficial]. It is also referenced in collaborative neural radiance field implementations for novel view synthesis, where grid-based step sizes are calculated from AABB dimensions [S4, unofficial].
 
